# <type>[optional scope][!]: <subject>
#
# Conventional Commits (https://www.conventionalcommits.org). The type decides the next release
# (python-semantic-release, see pyproject.toml):
#   feat:      new feature or capability             -> minor release
#   fix:       bug fix                                -> patch release
#   perf:      performance improvement                -> patch release
#   docs:      documentation only                     -> no release
#   refactor:  code change that is not a feat or fix  -> no release
#   test:      tests only                             -> no release
#   build:     packaging, dependencies, Docker images -> no release
#   ci:        GitHub Actions workflows               -> no release
#   chore:     anything else (repo housekeeping)      -> no release
# A `!` after the type/scope or a "BREAKING CHANGE: ..." footer makes a major release.
#
# Subject: imperative mood, lowercase, no period at the end, at most 72 chars.
# Body (optional): what and why, wrapped at 72 chars.
# Footer (optional): BREAKING CHANGE: ..., Closes #123
#
# Example:
#   feat(run): add --fat-image option
#
#   Lets the emulator mount a FAT image as the SD card of the NDS.
#
#   Closes #123
